  "description": "Train positions on the track network (the network counterpart of train-position.json, ARCHITECTURE decision 51). Nodes 1 (1024, 2048) to 4 (4096, 2048) a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 to e3 of 1024; e4 runs from node 3 south to node 5 (3072, 3072) and, leaving node 3 at a right angle, joins neither e2 nor e3; e5 runs alone from node 6 (6144, 3072) to node 7 (6144, 4096). Track costs 1000 a tile of edge, five edges here. New trains are unplaced. A train of one car stands on an edge, going forward or backward, at any offset from 0 to the edge's length (its ends included, so also at a node or a dead end); an unknown edge, a negative offset and one past the end are invalidTrainPosition. placeTrain checks unknownTrain, trainAlreadyPlaced, then the position; reverseTrain and unplaceTrain check unknownTrain, then trainNotPlaced. Reversing a train of one car keeps its place and turns its way: the offset becomes the edge's length less the offset (256 forward becomes 768 backward, the end of e5 forward becomes its start backward), and reversing twice restores it. An edge with a train's head (or body) on it cannot be removed (trackEdgeInUse), also with the train standing at its end; a train at the start of e3, at node 3, stands on e3 only, so e2, which ends at node 3, can be removed while it stands there, and e3 once it is unplaced; a node can be removed only when no edge ends at it (trackNodeInUse). Placement is free, removal is not refunded, and with every rate 0 time passing at any speed, or paused, moves no train.",
